.TH WALLPICKER 1
.SH NAME
wallpicker \- interactive wallpaper selector with hexagonal thumbnail UI
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B wallpicker
.br
.B wallpicker
.I directory
.br
.B wallpicker
[\fB\-c\fR \fIn\fR]
[\fB\-s\fR \fIpx\fR]
[\fB\-a\fR \fIdeg\fR]
[\fB\-C\fR \fIpath\fR]
[\fB\-t\fR]
[\fIdirectory\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B wallpicker
is an interactive utility for producing wallpaper selections.
It operates on a directory of images and produces a transparent, undecorated raylib window containing a hexagonal grid of thumbnails.

The thumbnails are generated deterministically and cached as follows:
On the first run, supported images are resized, clipped to a hexagonal mask, and written to the cache directory.
Cache identity includes the source file and thumbnail recipe, so changing an image or the grid angle generates a fresh thumbnail.
Subsequent executions load directly from matching cache entries.

Clicking a thumbnail computes the relative X and Y screen coordinates of the selection and tries to execute the runtime hook.
If no hook exists, it falls back to a minimal built-in apply logic.
.SH OPTIONS
Command-line values override the runtime file, which overrides built-in defaults.
Invalid options or values are errors.
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-cols " " \fIn\fR
Arrange thumbnails in \fIn\fR columns.
\fIn\fR must be a positive integer.
.TP
.BR \-s ", " \-\-spacing " " \fIpx\fR
Set the gap between adjacent hexagons to \fIpx\fR pixels.
\fIpx\fR must be a non-negative number.
.TP
.BR \-a ", " \-\-angle " " \fIdeg\fR
Rotate the grid layout by \fIdeg\fR degrees clockwise.
.TP
.BR \-C ", " \-\-config " " \fIpath\fR
Load this required runtime TOML file instead of the automatically selected file.
.TP
.BR \-t ", " \-\-check-config
Validate configuration, print the effective settings as TOML, and exit.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print usage and exit without reading configuration files.
.TP
.I directory
A single optional positional argument specifying the directory to scan for wallpaper images.
.SH CONFIGURATION
The session selects runtime-wayland.toml or runtime-x11.toml below
$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/hypr-wallpicker/runtime.
An unset, empty or relative XDG_CONFIG_HOME falls back to $HOME/.config.
XDG_SESSION_TYPE (wayland or x11) takes precedence, followed by
WAYLAND_DISPLAY and DISPLAY. An unknown session skips automatic loading.
Missing automatic files use defaults; other read or validation errors are fatal.
.PP
The TOML schema requires integer schema_version = 1.
Optional tables are [wallpaper] (directory) and [renderer] (cols, spacing, angle).
Unknown fields and invalid types are rejected.
Directory must be absolute or start with ~/; only the latter expands HOME.
CLI directories may be relative; they are anchored to the current working
directory without checking existence or collapsing symlinks or .. components.
Empty paths are rejected. Printed configuration can be read back with --config.
Columns must fit a positive C int; spacing and angle must be finite C floats,
and spacing must be non-negative. Nonzero values that underflow to zero during
conversion are rejected in both TOML and CLI input.
Configuration is read once at startup. Presets, config.toml compilation,
engine selection and post-hooks are not implemented by this loader.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $HOME/Pictures/wallpapers
Default wallpaper directory.
.TP
.I $XDG_CACHE_HOME/wallpicker/thumbnails-v2
Cache directory for hex-masked thumbnails. If
.B XDG_CACHE_HOME
is unset, this resolves to
.I $HOME/.cache/wallpicker/thumbnails-v2.
.TP
.I $HOME/.config/hypr-wallpicker/apply-wallpaper.sh
Runtime hook path.
Executed on selection with three positional arguments:
.B $1
(wallpaper path),
.B $2
(rel_x),
.B $3
(rel_y).
.PP
The source repository ships with examples (e.g., \fIscripts/apply-wallpaper-wayland.example.sh\fR).
These are examples only and are not auto-installed runtime hooks.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
Base directory for runtime configuration only. The legacy hook path is unchanged.
.TP
.B HOME
Required by \fBwallpicker\fR to resolve the default wallpaper directory, cache directory, and runtime hook path.
.TP
.B XDG_CACHE_HOME
Optional base directory for the thumbnail cache.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Normal success.
.TP
.B 2
Invalid command-line options or runtime configuration.
.TP
.B 1
Initialization, path resolution, memory allocation, setup, or stdout write failure.
.SH EXAMPLES
Launch with the default wallpaper directory:
.PP
.RS
.B wallpicker
.RE
.PP
Launch with a specific directory:
.PP
.RS
.B wallpicker
.I ~/Pictures/wallpapers
.RE
.PP
Launch with an absolute path and custom grid layout:
.PP
.RS
.B wallpicker
\fB\-c\fR 6 \fB\-a\fR 15.0
.I /mnt/media/walls
.RE
.SH NOTES
The built-in fallback logic is intentionally minimal right now.
It only conditionally attempts to execute
.BR awww (1)
if the binary is present in the system path.
All legacy post-commands (such as symlinking, matugen execution, and hyprland reloads) are currently commented out in the source code.

Custom hooks are the intended portability path for handling differences between Wayland and X11 environments for now.

Official documentation and updates can be found at the project repository:
.UR https://github.com/Horizon0427/hypr-wallpicker
.UE
